Pi adaptation: local_process.rs owns a shared one-second, monotonic output-drain
deadline after parent exit. Output activity cannot reset it. Both stream readers
finish before Closed is emitted; ordinary EOF still closes immediately. The
TypeScript bridge waits for Closed rather than inferring closure from silence.
This is a local-only helper, not Codex's remote execution transport. Process
retention, cancellation and TTY policies remain local and unchanged.

Pi's standalone dispatcher runs Read waits concurrently so silent processes do
not block other process output or mutation requests. Request IDs correlate
responses; stdout frames remain serialized. The TypeScript bridge serializes
reads per process before sequence capture/decoding, and the helper reaps read
tasks and aborts/joins outstanding waits on shutdown. Exec/write/terminate/shutdown
dispatch remains ordered. No output-buffer bound or upstream source pin changed.
